note bottom of trip_status_history
  trip_status_history and incidents are internal entities
  of the Trip aggregate. **ON DELETE CASCADE** because their
  lifecycle depends entirely on the aggregate root.
end note

note right of trips
  **Partial unique index (load_request_id)**
  WHERE status <> 'CANCELLED': a load request has at
  most one active trip; if the carrier cancels,
  the load is republished and another trip takes it (US55).
  --
  **CHECK status**: ASSIGNED, EN_ROUTE_TO_PICKUP,
  AT_PICKUP_POINT, CARGO_PICKED_UP, IN_TRANSIT,
  DELAYED, DELIVERED, DISPUTED, COMPLETED, CANCELLED
  --
  **CHECK**: CANCELLED requires reason and date;
  DISPUTED requires delivery_dispute_reason (US56).
end note

